    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0442" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg384"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Courtney</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 8, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose the original of a letter
                    addressed to me by a person signing himself Antonio Lopez de Santa Anna, and, as
                    you will see, claiming to be a nephew of the general of that name. My reply to
                    the same is also enclosed. It is desired that you should ascertain whether or
                    not there is such a person as the writer of the letter. If there should be, the
                    answer may be posted. If there should not be any such person, I will thank you
                    to return the letter and the reply to this department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Samuel</hi> G. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Courtney</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">Attorney of the United
                            States for the Southern District of New York</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d126-a1.xml" xpointer="d126-a1"/>
